{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "At work recently, we needed to introduce the concept of a queue into our rails app.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fc2be18250f810c78e8e99952e13041b0fc416aa0d77fe089050b5856aaa89d7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [3, 1.18, 1.28], [4, 1.28, 1.48], [5, 1.48, 1.66], [6, 1.66, 1.96], [7, 1.96, 2.14], [8, 2.14, 2.5], [9, 2.5, 2.74], [10, 2.74, 2.82], [12, 3.04, 3.36], [13, 3.36, 3.52], [14, 3.52, 3.72], [15, 3.72, 4.1]]}, {"text": "MySQL really doesn’t do a great job with these types of things, because it is so slow.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7c83894f6460ccbaae5aecc81ae1098607f81362e0bbea63448e21eb161a9629.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.52, 0.86], [2, 0.86, 1.2], [3, 1.2, 1.36], [4, 1.36, 1.46], [5, 1.46, 1.64], [6, 1.64, 1.92], [7, 1.92, 2.12], [8, 2.12, 2.28], [9, 2.28, 2.48], [10, 2.48, 2.66], [11, 2.66, 3.02], [12, 3.02, 3.62], [13, 3.62, 3.78], [14, 3.78, 3.9], [15, 3.9, 4.1], [16, 4.1, 4.4]]}, {"text": "Redis is a much better solution, because its speed and ease of use.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9193953abc844b5d15bf6837a51854dcda9af6975512792a22d1678eb2e80448.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.44, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.64], [3, 0.64, 0.78], [4, 0.78, 0.98], [5, 0.98, 1.46], [6, 1.46, 1.96], [7, 1.96, 2.22], [8, 2.22, 2.44], [9, 2.44, 2.74], [10, 2.74, 2.92], [11, 2.92, 3.04], [12, 3.04, 3.26]]}, {"text": "I built the queueing concern on top of RedisObjects, because it has such a great DSL wrapper for storing ruby types into redis.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/610539f4aeadc18d877176657e9d58ca08e900a173e3efc092a39782f8c4c7db.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [2, 0.5, 0.64], [4, 0.9, 1.26], [5, 1.26, 1.48], [6, 1.48, 1.66], [7, 1.66, 1.9], [9, 2.5, 2.88], [10, 2.88, 3.06], [11, 3.06, 3.2], [12, 3.2, 3.48], [13, 3.48, 3.58], [14, 3.58, 3.82], [15, 3.82, 4.38], [16, 4.38, 4.64], [17, 4.64, 4.94], [18, 4.94, 5.3], [19, 5.3, 5.54], [20, 5.54, 5.9], [21, 5.9, 6.22], [22, 6.22, 6.66]]}, {"text": "The main feature I use is their list object.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ab9677bee820e14d64c30e4c0e47afbb02306b37eb06333b4aadcc19be163e9c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.12], [1, 0.12, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.76], [4, 0.76, 1.06], [5, 1.06, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.5], [7, 1.5, 1.76], [8, 1.76, 2.28]]}, {"text": "```ruby queueable.rb module Queueable extend ActiveSupport::Concern", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d6824913a1691cf4a9bf98978e0652de2af53a7d2aa8c44669d7d94e189199a9.mp3"}, {"text": "included do include Redis::Objects end", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/84a074265b0a8f5da30e604eeef411ee8b73006709bf7bae20ff32c3dce4ea68.mp3"}, {"text": "# more code here", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e9d407c8f119ba00085f44de215ddff8bfe78503c5d5f04522ffa61b76d3dfba.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.0, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.98]]}, {"text": "end", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/940bb3913e4a6d466b772ec7cf440dec964b0e0551a5294b53284a8004259eb9.mp3"}, {"text": "For the purposes of my application, I needed to be able to:", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/be4e1bc9b6db37c59db41fb58aa8f9a067520850fa288c28921bdf4f71e0826c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.68], [3, 0.68, 0.9], [4, 0.9, 1.02], [5, 1.02, 1.56], [6, 2.14, 2.24], [7, 2.24, 2.48], [8, 2.48, 2.64], [9, 2.64, 2.76], [10, 2.76, 2.98], [11, 2.98, 3.28]]}, {"text": "rotate the queue, such that the top element returned and is moved to the bottom of the queue.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/98a7aacdf3715c232b1feedce4bfd939283c5e7cae411655602aba8c9b39d3fb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.44], [1, 0.44, 0.58], [3, 0.86, 1.36], [4, 1.36, 1.56], [5, 1.56, 1.68], [6, 1.68, 1.88], [7, 1.88, 2.3], [8, 2.3, 2.78], [9, 2.78, 3.08], [10, 3.08, 3.24], [11, 3.24, 3.46], [12, 3.46, 3.7], [13, 3.7, 3.8], [14, 3.8, 4.08], [15, 4.08, 4.28], [16, 4.28, 4.38]]}, {"text": "set the entire queue to something new.", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/983a3fd5e9d5b78a69d21526056ece95a94f712bf2a7bfc27d082e5d2b52cf60.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.24], [5, 1.24, 1.54], [6, 1.54, 1.84]]}, {"text": "re-queue a element, so that if it exists in my queue, it gets sent to the bottom.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7c3304f2bc87cf1f96944ccb97ca40cbcb7bff93955a78008db74a58fe46aa9e.mp3", "words": [[3, 0.76, 1.22], [4, 1.22, 1.34], [5, 1.34, 1.5], [6, 1.5, 1.56], [7, 1.56, 1.84], [8, 1.84, 2.12], [9, 2.12, 2.26], [12, 2.8, 2.94], [13, 2.94, 3.16], [14, 3.16, 3.34], [15, 3.34, 3.42], [16, 3.42, 3.68]]}, {"text": "```ruby user_controller.rb class UserController < ActiveController::Base def show user = User.find(params[:id]) next_score = user.rotate_scoring_queue #gets the top element and moves it to the bottom user.requeue_scoring_queue invited_score # moves this score to the bottom of the queue end end", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6b0e64043f03a569ff380e50ccddbd22d51ec4d1ae7eef8b197f9f69145dc6af.mp3"}, {"text": "The first line def queue adds in my DSL method to the model to allow queues with a given name to be created.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f1ed9b4bfb389e795bc998062d30974a0619b6f916528a96312f7d730fd8be51.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.44], [5, 1.1, 1.5], [7, 1.86, 2.04], [8, 2.04, 2.58], [9, 2.58, 2.84], [10, 2.84, 3.08], [11, 3.08, 3.16], [12, 3.16, 3.42], [13, 3.42, 3.72], [14, 3.72, 3.96], [15, 3.96, 4.38], [16, 4.38, 4.48], [17, 4.48, 4.58], [18, 4.58, 4.78], [19, 4.78, 5.06], [20, 5.06, 5.3], [21, 5.3, 5.38], [22, 5.38, 5.76]]}, {"text": "Unfortunately RedisObjects doesn’t come with an out of the box way to set an entire list at once.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c3e2b81c2fc5b40193755cafe1b416733c3468342e6c83e8b5af696aa5bbb8eb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.66], [2, 1.66, 1.92], [3, 1.92, 2.08], [4, 2.08, 2.26], [5, 2.26, 2.4], [6, 2.4, 2.58], [7, 2.58, 2.7], [8, 2.7, 2.8], [9, 2.8, 2.98], [10, 2.98, 3.32], [11, 3.32, 3.5], [12, 3.5, 3.68], [13, 3.68, 3.84], [14, 3.84, 4.2], [15, 4.2, 4.48], [16, 4.48, 4.62], [17, 4.62, 4.88]]}, {"text": "So I had to write my own using Redis transactions.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d2fe073bab54503e82051f36e4f48b6e9365f55dbaa3d873a103636e16115465.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.28], [2, 0.28, 0.4], [3, 0.4, 0.52], [4, 0.52, 0.64], [5, 0.64, 0.82], [6, 0.82, 0.98], [7, 0.98, 1.3], [9, 1.7, 2.24]]}, {"text": "So the second method overrides the setter method of the list to accept an array of values that we will set.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/eb64f65609b6e74221687f992a5c6e03141f47d6b1d7bbf7cb606bfa7133485b.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.28], [2, 0.28, 0.58], [3, 0.58, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.82], [5, 1.82, 2.0], [6, 2.0, 2.34], [7, 2.34, 2.62], [8, 2.62, 2.86], [9, 2.86, 3.04], [10, 3.04, 3.34], [11, 3.34, 3.64], [12, 3.64, 3.96], [14, 4.18, 4.42], [15, 4.42, 4.6], [16, 4.6, 4.92], [17, 4.92, 5.18], [18, 5.18, 5.32], [19, 5.32, 5.44], [20, 5.44, 5.66]]}, {"text": "The re-queue method removes a target value from the queue.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/17afe5c6bdaedcf2edc2af745b12796a014e17f4e65888f64b6cddc642de9f90.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [2, 0.64, 1.02], [3, 1.02, 1.4], [4, 1.4, 1.66], [5, 1.66, 2.0], [6, 2.0, 2.34], [7, 2.34, 2.6], [8, 2.6, 2.76]]}, {"text": "Then it sets it to the queue, if it can’t find a last item (then that means it was the only item in the queue), it adds it back to the list.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/eb60b77bc257d8d7f0928498ef997c9905674e5aff8bdcd78698095ed85130b0.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.52], [3, 0.52, 0.7], [4, 0.7, 0.82], [5, 0.82, 0.94], [6, 0.94, 1.2], [8, 1.58, 1.7], [9, 1.7, 1.92], [10, 1.92, 2.1], [11, 2.1, 2.26], [12, 2.26, 2.48], [13, 2.48, 2.8], [14, 3.24, 3.46], [15, 3.46, 3.64], [16, 3.64, 3.82], [17, 3.82, 4.12], [18, 4.12, 4.22], [19, 4.22, 4.36], [20, 4.36, 4.54], [21, 4.54, 4.8], [22, 4.8, 4.94], [23, 4.94, 5.04], [24, 5.04, 5.3], [25, 5.7, 5.88], [26, 5.88, 6.04], [27, 6.04, 6.14], [28, 6.14, 6.3], [29, 6.3, 6.48], [30, 6.48, 6.6], [31, 6.6, 6.94]]}]}